<title>HONG KONG: Morgan Stanley cuts Thailand, Hong Kong weightings.</title>
<headline>Morgan Stanley cuts Thailand, Hong Kong weightings.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. broker Morgan Stanley said it cut weightings for Thailand and Hong Kong in its model portfolio last Thursday in response to expectations of a rise in U.S. interest rates.  </p>
<p>&quot;(We) are concerned about a possible rise in U.S. interest rates,&quot; said Morgan Stanley spokesman Wesley McDade.</p>
<p>&quot;Such a rise is likely to lead to short-term weakness in Southeast Asian markets.&quot;</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley regional stratgist Peter Churchouse increased the cash weighting in his model portfolio to 15 percent from 10 percent last Thursday, McDade said.</p>
<p>Hong Kong's weighting dropped to 20.5 percent from 23.0 percent while Thailand's weighting was cut to 6.5 percent from 9.0 percent.</p>
<p>--Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
